### Inject queue into a service with @InjectQueue

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/queues.md

Inject a BullMQ queue instance into a NestJS provider. The `@InjectQueue()` decorator identifies the queue by the name passed to `registerQueue()`.

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { Queue } from 'bullmq';
import { InjectQueue } from '@nestjs/bullmq';

@Injectable()
export class AudioService {
  constructor(@InjectQueue('audio') private audioQueue: Queue) {}
}
```

