### Declare a BullMQ consumer class with @Processor

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/queues.md

Decorate a class with @Processor to define a queue consumer for a specific queue. Consumers must be registered as NestJS providers so @nestjs/bullmq can pick them up.

```typescript
import { Processor } from '@nestjs/bullmq';

@Processor('audio')
export class AudioConsumer {}
```

