### Process queue jobs by extending WorkerHost

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/queues.md

Extend WorkerHost and implement the process() method to handle jobs when the worker is idle. The value returned by process() is stored on the job object and accessible in completed event listeners.

```typescript
import { Processor, WorkerHost } from '@nestjs/bullmq';
import { Job } from 'bullmq';

@Processor('audio')
export class AudioConsumer extends WorkerHost {
  async process(job: Job<any, any, string>): Promise<any> {
    let progress = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
      await doSomething(job.data);
      progress += 1;
      await job.updateProgress(progress);
    }
    return {};
  }
}
```

